  "description": "CR 303.4e whole cards: Aura Graft takes bob's Control Magic and the creature it moves onto",
  "note": "CR 303.4e: an Aura's controller is separate from the enchanted object's, so gaining the Aura and moving it are two changes, and Control Magic's static ability then hands the NEW host to the Aura's new controller (CR 613.1b). Three permanents change hands off one spell: alice takes the Aura, takes the Mammoth it lands on, and gets her own Piker back. bob's second Piker makes the destination a real choice. CR 302.6: alice has not controlled the Mammoth since her turn began, so she cannot attack with it, and with her Piker just regained neither can attack: no attack declaration is asked, and an unscheduled one would fail the run. The Haskell read that the Aura itself is re-Sicked is dropped: CR 302.6 speaks only of creatures, so no board observes it.",
